Z||000000||Ferrari355||02-03-2000||05:44 PM||||I am having trouble with my headlights on the fiero, it is an 84 SE. ok, one will go down but won't come up and the other doesn't go down at all, i need help. they are both getting power and the motors seem like they are in good shape, do you think it could be a realy. And sometimes if you flip the light switch on the dash quickly the motor will spin alittle. If yuo can give me any info on this it would be really great. Thanks, Alex... Yuo can e-mail me at  <A HREF="mailto:Alexb2004@aol.com">Alexb2004@aol.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ggarsk||02-03-2000||06:02 PM||||If the motor spins without moving the it most likely meams that you have a stripped gear. As for the relays,you have 3 relays. One each for each motor and a different one(isolater relay) for both motors. You can try switching the right and left side relays to see if that helps. I've found out with headlights it's trial and error till you get it right. Goodluck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||02-03-2000||07:30 PM||||I have the sam problem on my Fiero, one will go down but not up...I'm pretty sure it's an accutor switch (i cant spell) but it's the small black box thing that the main 2 plugs plug into on the side of the head light assembly.  Try switching thoes or buy new one and they should work fine.||||reg||7
